From c2b89eb678a49cb1f77a77b625dab85150e9726f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:22:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(update): an agent cron turn no longer refuses
 every instant checkpoint of its run

A cron_cut instant update tolerates confirmed Kanban workers plus the cron runs it
cuts. An agent cron job (kanban-hub-pin-sweep, hourly, ~11 min) also executes its
turn on the session owner, so the gateway total counted it twice: once as the
scheduler run and once as an authority turn. checkpoint_for_update then saw one
unit of unknown work and refused every attempt for the whole run.

hermes-hub 2026-11-12 10:36-10:39Z: six refused update runs, each with the
gateway reporting exactly one unit more than managed Kanban sessions + cron runs
(10 vs 7+2, 9 vs 6+2); the passing runs at 10:51, 11:05 and 11:14 had no agent
cron in flight and matched exactly.

cron_turn_count() counts executing authority turns whose frozen policy source is
cron, each session once and only in a bucket the total counts; an unreadable
policy is not a cron turn (fail closed). The checkpoint verb and the restart
wait's Kanban/cron cap add it under a cron_cut intent only.
